{"sourceSha256": "fb3e4f53915d6afb4ad20f0e500a9c15a2c7d2cacb6f5c9a3f87d095a1347fce", "text": "Dear Doctor,\nRe: Mr Fred Davies, Agec 65\n\nam writing to request on urgent hospital admission for Mr Davies who presented today\nwith symptoms suggestive of acute colonic pseudo obstruction for which he requires\nassessment and further investigations.\n\nMr Davies attended the Emergency Department complaining of a four-day history of severe\nabdominal distension associated with nausea, poor appetite and generalised abdominal\npain. Despite passing flatulence, his last bowel action was 5 cays ago. On examination, he\n\nhad a dry mouth and difficulty in lying tn a supine position. His vital signs were\nunremarkable apart from tachycardia and low oxygen saturation on room air. His abdominal\nexamination revealed a marked distension with diffuse tenderness. However, no rebound\ntenderness or guarding was detected and his bowel sounds were tympanic.\n\nMr Davies’ test results showed elevated white blood cells counts together with high blood\nurea and aspartate aminotransferase levels, while other laboratory values were normal. His\nX-ray indicated significant dilatation tn the cecum as well as in the ascending and\n\ntransverse colon.\n\nBased on the above. | would be grateful if you could arrange a CT scan of the abdomen and\n\npelvis and consider the possibility of surgical management if required. If you have any\nqueries, please do not hesitate to contact me.\n\nYours sincerely,\nDoctor", "pages": [{"number": 1, "text": "Dear Doctor,\nRe: Mr Fred Davies, Agec 65\n\nam writing to request on urgent hospital admission for Mr Davies who presented today\nwith symptoms suggestive of acute colonic pseudo obstruction for which he requires\nassessment and further investigations.\n\nMr Davies attended the Emergency Department complaining of a four-day history of severe\nabdominal distension associated with nausea, poor appetite and generalised abdominal\npain. Despite passing flatulence, his last bowel action was 5 cays ago. On examination, he\n\nhad a dry mouth and difficulty in lying tn a supine position. His vital signs were\nunremarkable apart from tachycardia and low oxygen saturation on room air. His abdominal\nexamination revealed a marked distension with diffuse tenderness. However, no rebound\ntenderness or guarding was detected and his bowel sounds were tympanic.\n\nMr Davies’ test results showed elevated white blood cells counts together with high blood\nurea and aspartate aminotransferase levels, while other laboratory values were normal. His\nX-ray indicated significant dilatation tn the cecum as well as in the ascending and\n\ntransverse colon.\n\nBased on the above. | would be grateful if you could arrange a CT scan of the abdomen and\n\npelvis and consider the possibility of surgical management if required. If you have any\nqueries, please do not hesitate to contact me.\n\nYours sincerely,\nDoctor", "extraction": "ocr", "layout": {"version": 1, "width": 2422.0, "height": 2800.0, "blocks": [{"text": "Dear Doctor,\nRe: Mr Fred Davies, Agec 65", "lines": [{"text": "Dear Doctor,", "x": 0.00991, "y": 0.00679, "width": 0.13254, "height": 0.02214, "confidence": 0.93, "words": [{"text": "Dear", "x": 0.00991, "width": 0.05161, "confidence": 0.962}, {"text": "Doctor,", "x": 0.07143, "width": 0.07102, "confidence": 0.897}], "uncertainWords": []}, {"text": "Re: Mr Fred Davies, Agec 65", "x": 0.01156, "y": 0.05107, "width": 0.29727, "height": 0.02214, "confidence": 0.92, "words": [{"text": "Re:", "x": 0.01156, "width": 0.0322, "confidence": 0.961}, {"text": "Mr", "x": 0.05656, "width": 0.02395, "confidence": 0.942}, {"text": "Fred", "x": 0.08877, "width": 0.045, "confidence": 0.957}, {"text": "Davies,", "x": 0.14121, "width": 0.16639, "confidence": 0.918}, {"text": "Agec", "x": 0.23163, "width": 0.04294, "confidence": 0.789}, {"text": "65", "x": 0.28489, "width": 0.02395, "confidence": 0.954}], "uncertainWords": []}]}, {"text": "am writing t